After uploading the BRD, the system prompts the user to enter a password (empty password via pop-up). The expected behavior is that the system must pause execution and wait indefinitely until the user provides the password input.
Currently, the system waits only for 30 seconds and then automatically proceeds to read/process the output file, even if the password has not been entered. This behavior is incorrect.
Required behavior:
The system must not proceed automatically after any timeout.
It should strictly wait for user input (password submission) before continuing.
Only after the password is entered (even if empty), the system should proceed to the next step (e.g., reading or processing the output file).
Goal: Ensure a blocking/wait state is maintained until explicit user action (password input) is completed, with no auto-timeout fallback.
